(7350764, 1147975, 135744, '<td valign="top">Such super colours. I would have had to give this a good dose of the oil painting filter and get a DQ but it would be worth it<br/> <br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=1149918" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/135000-139999/135744/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1149918.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/135000-139999/135744/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1149918.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/135000-139999/135744/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1149918.jpg"/></a></td>', 'Such super colours. I would have had to give this a good dose of the oil painting filter and get a DQ but it would be worth it ', '2015-05-15 12:29:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(7350926, 1147993, 100831, '<td valign="top">Congrats on the top ten placement!</td>', 'Congrats on the top ten placement!', '2015-05-16 14:49:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(7387462, 1148047, 46918, '<td valign="top">Hello from the critique club...<br/> <br/>Nice finish. I have been looking at this shot for like 30 min and I''m sorry but I just don''t see anything resembling a fish. I did not vote but I probably would have been one of those DNMC voters we all hate. On to the actual picture now. The shot is good for an abstract I do like it even though I think it is a DNMC. In fact, I could see this hanging on the wall. I like the flowing movements and the colors. Nice shot. Happy shooting.</td>', 'Hello from the critique club... Nice finish. I have been looking at this shot for like 30 min and I''m sorry but I just don''t see anything resembling a fish. I did not vote but I probably would have been one of those DNMC voters we all hate. On to the actual picture now. The shot is good for an abstract I do like it even though I think it is a DNMC. In fact, I could see this hanging on the wall. I like the flowing movements and the colors. Nice shot. Happy shooting.', '2015-07-15 12:53:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(7387514, 1147975, 25024, '<td valign="top">*Hello from Sid and the Critique Club*<br/> <br/>I must admit, whilst obviously, I''ve heard of MC Escher I had not heard of his three worlds so I had to google it, delightful. A competent image that meets the challenge and should have scored better, It certainly doesnt deserve all those sub fours.<br/> <br/>I really don''t think you have a problem with the focus, you have to accept that you are shooting through water which inevitably is not going to give you the same sharpness as air. At least you have managed to avoid the common problem in this situation of focussing on the waters surface which certainly would have rendered the fish soft. If you manage to come up with the magic formula in post-processing that will render unsharp images sharp then I will be delighted to hear from you. <br/> <br/>As you rightly point out the ''pollen'' on the waters surface is distracting and would benefit from removal and it may be this alone that has resulted in its lower than deserved score. I know its removal would have been tedious but I think it would have been worthwhile. Perhaps a quicker approach would have been to select these with colour range and simply subdue them thus making them much less conspicuous.<br/> <br/>I like the dynamic shape and the dorsal fin just breaking the surface, I like its vivid colouring, I like the distorted reflections from the ripples, the reflections themselves are not too bad either, shame there weren''t the leaves to complete your homage but a very good attempt I would say.<br/> <br/>Happy fishing Sid</td>', '*Hello from Sid and the Critique Club* I must admit, whilst obviously, I''ve heard of MC Escher I had not heard of his three worlds so I had to google it, delightful. A competent image that meets the challenge and should have scored better, It certainly doesnt deserve all those sub fours. I really don''t think you have a problem with the focus, you have to accept that you are shooting through water which inevitably is not going to give you the same sharpness as air. At least you have managed to avoid the common problem in this situation of focussing on the waters surface which certainly would have rendered the fish soft. If you manage to come up with the magic formula in post-processing that will render unsharp images sharp then I will be delighted to hear from you.  As you rightly point out the ''pollen'' on the waters surface is distracting and would benefit from removal and it may be this alone that has resulted in its lower than deserved score. I know its removal would have been tedious but I think it would have been worthwhile. Perhaps a quicker approach would have been to select these with colour range and simply subdue them thus making them much less conspicuous. I like the dynamic shape and the dorsal fin just breaking the surface, I like its vivid colouring, I like the distorted reflections from the ripples, the reflections themselves are not too bad either, shame there weren''t the leaves to complete your homage but a very good attempt I would say. Happy fishing Sid', '2015-07-15 13:52:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(7387589, 1147835, 46918, '<td valign="top">Hello from the critique club....<br/> <br/>Hey nice fish... I like the composure. Your crop is nice. The texture of the water and the fish''s scales is nice. The lighting, I think, is a bit bright on the fish''s underbelly. Some color has been lost. Not a bad shot. Happy shooting.</td>', 'Hello from the critique club.... Hey nice fish... I like the composure. Your crop is nice. The texture of the water and the fish''s scales is nice. The lighting, I think, is a bit bright on the fish''s underbelly. Some color has been lost. Not a bad shot. Happy shooting.', '2015-07-15 15:25:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(7617648, 1147973, 3306, '<td valign="top">What, no horseradish?</td>', 'What, no horseradish?', '2019-03-06 21:02:55.000000', NULL, 0);
